section('scope','Scope and evidence',p('Inventory of the real A4000TX at <strong>10.0.0.40</strong>, collected over its AmigaBridge connection on <strong>7 October 2026</strong> (Mac clock). This is a live hardware/OS inventory, supported by prior installation records and clearly identified manufacturer specifications.')+p('<strong>No persistent Amiga configuration, firmware or installed application was changed.</strong> Read-only queries and two small native inventory programs were staged in RAM:; their outputs were copied to this Mac. The disk inquiries were limited to mounted devices and used INQUIRY and READ CAPACITY. No media scan, format, repair, benchmark, reboot or audio playback was performed.')+p('“Live” means reported by this running machine. “Owner” means supplied in the conversation. “Specification” describes a product family, not a physical inspection. “Prior verification” records earlier tests, not a new test today. Unidentified revisions, serials and chip markings remain unknown. This report is an inventory, not a full disk backup.')+p('Collected: <code>'+H(now)+'</code>. Free-memory, task, socket and disk-usage figures are snapshots taken at different points during collection, while ScummVM was running. 1 MiB = 1,048,576 bytes; 1 GiB = 1,073,741,824 bytes; decimal GB = 1,000,000,000 bytes.'))
