section('storage','Physical drives, partitions and filesystems',tab(['Driver / unit','Reported identity','Revision','Capacity geometry','Raw capacity','Mounted volumes','Type'],phys)+p('The CF identification is based on the live drive model and '+link(source_urls['cf'],'SanDisk’s SDCFXS product specification')+'. Inquiry data is translated through the Buddha IDE driver. No drive serial was returned by the optional VPD query; firmware strings may be truncated. The SD adapter identifies itself rather than the card behind it. Both devices are solid-state media; the label “HDD50Gig” does not identify a rotating hard drive.')+tab(['Volume','DOS device','Driver','Filesystem','Registered version','Usable GiB','Used GiB','Free GiB','State'],[[*v[:5],f'{v[5]/1048576:.3f}',f'{v[6]/1048576:.3f}',f'{v[7]/1048576:.3f}',v[8]] for v in volumes])+p('Mounted-volume figures are filesystem-reported usable space. Raw device capacity and cylinder extents include space the filesystem does not report as usable; these figures should not be substituted for one another. FileSystem.resource reports PFS3 19.2 and FFS 47.4; this identifies registered handlers, not a byte-for-byte verification of each disk’s RDB handler image.')+tab(['Partition','Cylinders','Heads × sectors/track','Extent GiB','Sectors/block','Buffers','MaxTransfer','Mask'],[
 ['BDH0','2–7742','16 × 68','4.0160','1 (default)','150','$00FFFFFF','$7FFFFFFE'],['BDH1','7743–114942','16 × 68','55.6152','8','150','$00FFFFFF','$7FFFFFFE'],['SDH0','2–39727','6 × 256','29.0962','2','80','$0001FE00','$7FFFFFFE']])+p('DF0: is mounted through trackdisk.device unit 0 with a 2-head, 80-cylinder, 11-sector default geometry (880 KiB DD layout); no disk was present. This does not establish the drive’s manufacturer or whether the mechanism supports HD media. RAM: is a dynamic memory filesystem, not a separate physical drive. No optical drive, SFS volume or USB mass-storage volume was mounted at this snapshot.')+details('MountInfo, Info and registered filesystem evidence',pre('info.txt')+''.join(pre('mount-'+n+'.txt') for n in ['BDH0','BDH1','SDH0','DF0'])+pre('filesystems.tsv')))
section('usb','USB ports and attached devices',p('The <strong>Freeway Triton Zorro III controller is active</strong>. The live startup log reports a root hub with <strong>three ports</strong>, successfully configured, with QuickIO enabled. The driver is <code>freewaytritonz3usb.device 1.01 (2022.05.16)</code>; Poseidon is <code>4.5 (14.10.2014)</code>. The host task and PIO transfer task are present.')+tab(['Property','Observed value'],[['Hub descriptor','Philips Semiconductors ISP1520'],['Vendor / product','0471 / 3526'],['USB version / reported speed','USB 2.00 / high-speed'],['Device address / class','Address 1; class 9, subclass 0, protocol 1 (single-TT hub)'],['Serial / device revision','n/a / 0000'],['External devices now','None enumerated'],['Driver mode','Zorro III EHCI / PIO'],['Stack persistence','S:User-Startup runs ENVARC:PsdStackloader'],['FAT media support','L:fat95 3.18, dated 1 March 2013; loaded when needed']])+p('The descriptor’s self-powered/0 mA fields do not measure available port current. The reported three ports do not identify which case connector corresponds to each port, nor prove every physical socket under load. '+link(source_urls['freeway'],'The supplier’s Freeway specification')+' describes three USB connectors and USB 2.0 support; USB signalling speed is not actual Amiga file-transfer throughput.')+p('The available Poseidon log contains severity-0 startup messages and no higher-severity errors. Its informal “blame” and “laugh” messages are normal class-loading text. USB storage was successfully used earlier according to the owner, but no storage stick is attached now. The earlier DrawBridge/USB floppy is historical and is not a mounted native floppy or USB mass-storage device in this snapshot.')+details('Loaded USB classes and versions',tab(['Class','Header version','Embedded ID/date'],usbclasses))+details('USB descriptor and event-log evidence',pre('usb-root.txt')+pre('usb-errors.txt')))
