section('network','Networking and remote access',tab(['Property','Live result'],[['Interface','x-surf-100; device x-surf-100.device unit 0'],['Driver','1.16 (3 September 2018)'],['MAC address','28:CD:4C:FF:F2:B2'],['IPv4 / mask','10.0.0.40 / 255.255.255.0'],['Binding','Dynamic (DHCP), according to Roadshow'],['Gateway','10.0.0.1'],['DNS','10.0.0.1 listed twice: dynamic and static'],['MTU / reported link speed','1500 bytes / 100,000,000 bits/s'],['TCP/IP stack','Roadshow 1.15; bsdsocket.library 4.364 (1 September 2023), 68020+ build'],['Roadie','1.3.9 (20 December 2021)'],['Listening TCP socket','0.0.0.0:2345'],['Connected bridge client','10.0.0.21:63432 → 10.0.0.40:2345'],['UDP sockets','None shown at snapshot'],['SFTP/FTP server','No separate listening SFTP/FTP socket shown; earlier file-transfer setup is not evidence of a running server now']])+p('The detailed snapshot reports <strong>886 buffer overruns</strong>, 1 dropped packet in its aggregate field, and separate in/out drop counters of 0/2. These counters have different meanings and are preserved verbatim. Connectivity is working; one cumulative snapshot cannot establish when the overruns occurred or whether they are increasing. A later comparison under a controlled transfer would clarify whether tuning is useful. No counters were reset.')+p('The DHCP lease date displayed as 10/10/2033 is not a reliable wall-clock reference because the Amiga clock differs from the Mac. The duplicate DNS address is a configuration redundancy, not proof of a service failure.')+details('Detailed interface and socket evidence',pre('interface.txt')+pre('sockets.txt')))
